      "content_license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "body": "There are 12 months in a year. It doesn&#39;t really matter if they have 28, 29, 30, or 31 days, does it? We say a month. My daily meds are prescribed a month at a time; the prescription states &quot;30 tablets&quot;, which makes me short by a day every other month or so. I don&#39;t really care. In medicine, as in life, a month is roughly 30 days. If a doctor tells a patient on February 1st that they have 3 months to live on, the patient usually doesn&#39;t ask, is that 89, 90, 91, or 92 days? Is that counting today?"
    },
